{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Why, etc.</b> The meaning: why should I still leave you in the land because of your numerous burnt offerings. The word שבעתי is in the manner of human speech, but the truth is, if I were hungry I would not tell you (Psalms 50:12)." "<b>Rams.</b> They are large." "<b>Fattened cattle.</b> A kind of cattle, larger than it, and its fat is forbidden. The Gaon [Saadia] said it is from the language of the Mishnah (Shabbat 24:3), like בריאים." "<b>Bulls and sheep.</b> They are small." "<b>And goats.</b> Large, and they are the he-goats that mount the flock (Genesis 31:10)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:24.270986372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}